@startuml SQ-09
title SQ-09 Joystick steering: prediction & reconciliation [C requirement / P netcode]
actor Player
participant "Own Client" as C
participant "Match Server" as MS
participant "Other Clients" as O
loop client frame
  Player -> C : joystick vector u (touch / mouse / stick / keys)
  C -> C : quantise u (int8 x,y); store input[seq]
  C -> C : PREDICT own top movement:\nF = Fmax*u*mobility*Stab(spin)*(1-stagger)
end
loop 30 Hz
  C -> MS : C2S_ControlInput {seq, tick, u, last 3 inputs} (unreliable-sequenced)
end
MS -> MS : clamp |u| <= 1, rate <= 60/s, role COMPETITOR (SEC-015)
MS -> MS : authoritative tick 60 Hz: steering + physics + collisions
loop 30 Hz
  MS -> C : S2C_Snapshot {tick, lastProcessedSeq[own], tops[]}
  MS -> O : S2C_Snapshot
end
C -> C : RECONCILE: reset own top to server state at tick,\nreplay inputs with seq > lastProcessedSeq;\nsmooth correction < 100 ms
O -> O : interpolate remote tops (~100 ms buffer)
note over C,MS : Collisions, spin loss, burst and skills are only\nconfirmed by the server (never final on client).
@enduml
